      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "To a THF (15.0 mL) solution of 2-(2,6-DippNHCH2)C8H5NH (0.25 g, 0.8 mmol) was added a THF (15.0 mL) solution of (Me3SiCH2)3Gd(THF) (0.56 g, 1.0 mmol; 1.25 equiv relative to ligand) at room temperature. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 h (faint yellow to yellow). Solvent was removed under reduced pressure and the residue extracted with hexane (15.0 mL). Yellow crystals were obtained at 0 °C. The O(CH2)5SiMe3 ligands arise from ring-opening of THF by CH2SiMe3; C–H activation at the 7-indolyl position is observed.",
